            <ArticleTitle>Giant coronary aneurysms in heart transplantation: an unusual presentation of cardiac allograft vasculopathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1367-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cardiac allograft vasculopathy is a leading cause of death during long-term follow-up of heart transplant recipients. We report 2 cases of cardiac allograft vasculopathy associated with giant coronary aneurysms. To our knowledge, these are the first reported cases of spontaneous giant coronary aneurysms in heart transplant recipients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
